WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.620
- If you wanted to get from here

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.450
in London to here in New York

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.210
in under two hours, you'd
need to be moving fast,

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.900
really fast, hypersonic to be precise.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.920
And that's exactly the aim

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.470
of aviation startups,
Destinus and Hermeus.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.670
Companies like these are aiming

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.380
to build passenger planes that will travel

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.780
at Mach 5 more than twice the speed

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.120
of Concorde, dramatically
reducing the amount

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.310
of time it would take to fly anywhere.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.140
Now, while these companies
have made progress

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.750
developing new engines, conducting tests

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.490
and signing contracts with partners,

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:31.380
right now their hypersonic dreams

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.433
are not quite there.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.920
So as always, we're going to look

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.420
at where these companies are now,

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.920
where they want to be in the future

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.080
and what they need to do to get there.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.210
But before we get into
that, I want to explain

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.920
to you how these companies plan

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.660
on flying hypersonically.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.010
Their aim is to create a new engine

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.860
by combining turbojets
with ramjet technology.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.330
Now, if that sounds familiar,

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.230
you might have seen it

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.063
in "Top Gun Maverick".

00:00:53.063 --> 00:00:54.900
- Transitioning to Scramjet.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.850
- [Host] Albeit with a faster Scramjet.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.350
But if you don't dunno
what any of that means,

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.270
I asked Hermeus's CEO to explain it

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.303
to me like I was a five year old.

00:01:05.303 --> 00:01:06.900
- You compress air, you burn it,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.370
and then you exhaust it through a nozzle

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:09.270
to generate thrust.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.770
On the turbojet side,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.210
you need a mechanical compressor

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:15.000
to compress the air and you need a turbine

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.020
to power the compressor.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.040
So with a ramjet,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.540
you compress it with a shockwave.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.580
So it's naturally done just based

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.780
on the speed that you're going.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.190
- [Host] That's why these companies plan

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.590
on using a combination of both engines,

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.210
a turbojet to take off

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.190
and get you fast enough or a ramjet

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.290
to kick in and take you hypersonic.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.420
And ramjet technology isn't new.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.820
It's actually been
proven to work years ago.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.100
- What we demonstrated today is something

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.050
that we've been working on in the ground

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.640
for over 40 years.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.473
- [Host] So now Destinus

00:01:42.473 --> 00:01:44.550
and Hermeus are hoping to use that tech

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.930
to carry passengers.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.280
- In 10, 15 years,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.280
you can have the first passenger plane,

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.910
not big one, not like Boeing 777,

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:56.220
kinda small one like (indistinct).

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.220
- [Host] That's Mikhail
Kokorich, CEO of Destinus

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.053
who hopes to have

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:03.000
its 25 seat Destinus S aircraft ready

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.490
for commercial service by 2030.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:06.870
And Hermeus aims to have

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.700
its 20 seat Halcyon aircraft

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:09.840
carrying paying passengers

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.280
by around the same time.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.450
- We're not so naive to think

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.220
that we could do that right off the bat.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.220
So we've laid out a
roadmap of three aircrafts

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.660
that will incrementally buy

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.710
down the technical risk

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.030
as well as the business risk.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.260
- [Host] As for the ticket costs,

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.210
well that will be down to the airline.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.880
But Hermeus told me
that much like Concorde,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.510
it could be charged at a premium price.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.040
But all of that is in the future.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.660
And right now, both of these companies

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:36.240
are a long way from carrying passengers.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.200
Both have been working

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.780
on that tricky turbojet ramjet problem

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.540
by taking existing engines
and modifying them.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.680
Destinus has also managed

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.540
to fly some test flights albeit

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.360
with smaller scale models,
with smaller engines.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.440
- After two and a half years,

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.180
we tested two prototypes.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.940
We are building the Supersonic prototype

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.470
which will be the first supersonic

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.520
manned vehicle in Europe.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.260
- And both companies
are using the knowledge

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.093
that they're gaining

00:02:59.093 --> 00:03:00.990
from pursuing hypersonic flight

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.730
to sell products and services.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.830
Hermeus plans to use
its development aircraft

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.020
as a test bed for the US military,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.410
signing a $60 million deal
with the US Air Force.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:11.730
- So for the flight test services that

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.290
that conducts we'll provide those

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.240
as a service to our customers

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.340
be they the US government allied partners

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.870
or industry.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.550
- But in order for these
companies to progress

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.720
from engine testing

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.150
to commercial hypersonic flight,

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:25.585
they're gonna have to find the solutions

00:03:25.585 --> 00:03:27.960
to a lot of unanswered questions.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.730
For starters, there are physics questions

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.250
like how to handle the
extreme temperatures

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.350
as the aircraft hits its top speed.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.430
There's also questions around

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.860
how passengers will
feel while accelerating

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.440
to Mach 5, because while these aircraft

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.270
won't go off like a rocket,

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.920
there still will be a sustained period

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.360
where you're accelerating.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.160
- So, the climb and acceleration period

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.740
on a hypersonic aircraft will last,

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.630
I'd say 12 to 15 minutes depending

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.530
on the trajectory.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.000
- [Host] Then there's
operational questions

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.760
like how to avoid creating
a sonic boom over land

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.310
and how that affects your
roots and scheduling.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.930
Destinus has told me
they'd still be quicker

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.580
than most flights, even if they had

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.920
to travel extra mileage to avoid land.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.290
- For hypersonic, when
you fly in 5,6 Mach,

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.587
it's like two hours and a half.

00:04:08.587 --> 00:04:09.420
It's the opposite.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.830
It's still extremely fast comparing

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.540
with the direct flight of 12 hours.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:13.373
- There's even questions

00:04:13.373 --> 00:04:15.420
around how regular
these flights would need

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.760
to be to become economically successful.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.200
After all, it's great saying

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.850
that you can fly from London to New York

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:23.310
in 90 minutes, but that's not much use

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.600
if the flight doesn't depart

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:25.770
for another six hours.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.020
And let's not forget,
we're now more connected

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.910
in the air than we've ever been before.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.080
And that means that the number

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.600
of people willing to
pay a premium to travel

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.490
at ultra fast speeds could be lower

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.330
than it used to be.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.753
All of that means that the economics

00:04:37.753 --> 00:04:39.510
around hypersonic flight

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.760
is still wildly uncertain.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.530
So for hypersonic flight to take off,

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.580
these companies are going to have

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.010
to develop their engines, flight test

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:48.480
and certify their aircraft,

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.090
receive regulatory approval
for their sonic boom

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.394
creating flight, establish route,

00:04:53.394 --> 00:04:55.860
prove that the experience can be safe

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.500
and comfortable and then
prove there's a market

00:04:58.500 --> 00:04:59.790
for hypersonic flight.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.680
That's a long road to be able

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.720
to carry paying passengers.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:04.980
So while these companies say

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.450
that this technology might be right

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.650
around the corner,

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.320
if you want to travel
somewhere hypersonically fast,

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.303
you might have to wait a while first.

00:05:13.295 --> 00:05:15.878
(upbeat music)

